now well many people love HOAs because  they keep neighborhoods nice but one  local homeowner says he's getting the  run around from his homeowners  association thank you so much for  staying with us here at 4 30 I'm  Christian Casas and I'm Kirsten Joyce  Mary Jane bellies shares one homeowner's  frustrations due to a landscaping  violation  a homeowner in a Northwest Valley  neighborhood is trying to stay in  compliance with his HOA but is having a  hard time getting answers so he reached  out to 8 news now I'm going to take out  the plants that are in there and put  them in the ground if I can Ryan  Gustafson first purchased his home in  2018 he's recently been hit this summer  with the Landscaping violation for not  having enough plants in his yard it's  been the same as the day I bought it  really so it'd suddenly be hit with this  violation there I feel like they're four  years late Gustafson says his HOA first  service residential is requiring a plan  for every 25 square feet of rock the  tree in his yard doesn't count as a  plant and potted plants aren't allowed  he says the HOA also hasn't specified  what types of plants he needs these are  things that I only learn by sending them  email after email trying to get more  information it's not clear anywhere in  their architectural guideline plan it's  not clear in the violation paperwork  that they gave me the plants must also  have a drip irrigation system system the  fact that we have to increase the amount  of water that we're pouring into our  yards at a time when our lake is at like  the biggest low that it's ever been at  just doesn't make any sense to me now a  few months later Gustafson is trying to  play catch-up after missing a few HOA  meetings he says he's trying to do the  best he can to follow their guidelines  and has reached out to his HOA on what  he needs to do if I'm in violation tell  me that I'm in violation of what I need  to do to fix it that should be the bare  minimum and what I'm finding is that  they can't seem to tell me what I need  to do in order to fix the problem  Gustafson says there is an HOA meeting  scheduled in October he plans to attend  so he can get clarification and that  could help his neighbors too reporting  from Durango and Cheyenne Mary Jane  beliesza 8 News Now
 

